  "id": "Compound::DB00394 - Gene::2908",
  "verbalization": "Beclomethasone is linked to Nr3c1 through a series of molecular interactions that ultimately converge on the glucocorticoid receptor (Nr3c1). The evidence suggests that Beclomethasone, through its binding to Serpina6 and Alclometasone, ultimately leads to the binding of Nr3c1. This pathway is consistent with the broader role of glucocorticoids in modulating gene expression, as both Beclomethasone and Budesonide are classified as therapeutic glucocorticoids. The shared ancestry of Beclomethasone and its metabolites with 21-hydroxy steroids further supports a common mechanism of action involving the glucocorticoid receptor. The integration of these pathways highlights the role of Nr3c1 in mediating the effects of glucocorticoids, with Beclomethasone acting as a precursor in the signaling cascade that regulates cellular responses to corticosteroids.",
